            "code": "```java\nprivate void remove(final InstructionHandle prev, InstructionHandle next) throws TargetLostException  {\n    final InstructionHandle first;\n    final InstructionHandle last;\n    // First and last deleted instruction if (prev == null && next == null)\n    {\n        first = start;\n        last = end;\n        start = end = null;\n    }\n    else\n    {\n        if (prev == null)\n        {\n            // At start of list first = start;\n            start = next;\n        }\n        else\n        {\n            first = prev.getNext();\n            prev.setNext(next);\n        }\n        if (next == null)\n        {\n            // At end of list last = end;\n            end = prev;\n        }\n        else\n        {\n            last = next.getPrev();\n            next.setPrev(prev);\n        }\n    }\n    first.setPrev(null);\n    // Completely separated from rest of list last.setNext(null);\n    final List<InstructionHandle> targetList = new ArrayList<>();\n    for (InstructionHandle ih = first;\n    ih != null;\n    ih = ih.getNext())\n    {\n        ih.getInstruction().dispose();\n        // for example BranchInstructions release their targets\n    }\n    final StringBuilder buf = new StringBuilder(\"\n    {\n        \");\n        for (InstructionHandle ih = first;\n        ih != null;\n        ih = next)\n        {\n            next = ih.getNext();\n            length--;\n            if (ih.hasTargeters())\n            {\n                // Still got targeters? targetList.add(ih);\n                buf.append(ih.toString(true)).append(\" \");\n                ih.setNext(ih.setPrev(null));\n            }\n            else\n            {\n                ih.dispose();\n            }\n        }\n        buf.append(\"\n    }\n    \");\n    if (!targetList.isEmpty())\n    {\n        throw new TargetLostException(targetList.toArray(InstructionHandle.EMPTY_ARRAY), buf.toString());\n    }\n}\n```"
